# Build context hygiene, and one deliberate guarantee.
#
# THE DELIBERATE PART: data/ticket_index*.faiss, data/ticket_metadata*.json and
# data/*.joblib are COMMITTED files, and they are excluded anyway. If they were
# copied in, the container could be serving the developer's artifacts while
# appearing to have built its own -- this project's recurring bug class exactly.
# Excluding them makes "the image built its own artifacts" a structural fact,
# and makes the adv_08 check in src/service/verify_deployment.py a real test of
# a from-scratch build.
#
# PATTERNS ARE ANCHORED AND `*` DOES NOT CROSS `/`.
# .dockerignore is matched with Go's filepath.Match against the whole relative
# path, so `*.npy` matches ONLY a .npy at the context root -- it does NOT match
# data/ticket_embeddings_bge-base-en-v1-5.npy. The first build of this image
# proved it the hard way: the developer's local 12 MB embedding cache was
# copied in, train_embeddings.py reported `[cache HIT]`, and the image's
# Tier-2 classifier and FAISS index were built from that cache instead of from
# its own encode. It ran clean and produced a plausible image -- the exact
# shape of this project's recurring bug, and occurrence #1 of it was a silent
# stale embedding cache. Nested patterns must be written `**/`.

# --- Never in an image -----------------------------------------------------
.env
venv/
.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- Local model artifacts: rebuilt inside the image ------------------------
models/
data/ticket_index*.faiss
data/ticket_metadata*.json
**/*.joblib
**/*.npy
**/*.npz

# --- Generated write-up surface: not a runtime dependency -------------------
paper/

# --- Bulk experiment data the service does not serve ------------------------
data/external_tobibueck/
data/category_stores/
data/skewed/
data/zeroshot_raw/
data/sufficiency_raw/
data/embedding_comparison/
data/batch_intake/
**/*.png
**/*.pdf

# --- Editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
**/Thumbs.db
**/.DS_Store
